1
00:00:02,810 --> 00:00:06,150
The sun is male, and represents a man...

2
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:09,230
And the moon is female; representing a woman.

3
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:14,200
When the sun and the moon come together, they become one...

4
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:17,370
...in other words, it represents a perfect being.{ok LOL}

5
00:00:18,330 --> 00:00:21,370
When they say "perfect being", are they talking about immortality?

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,620
My guess is that it's something even more incredible.

7
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:26,750
Like?

8
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:30,420
Like... God.

9
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:36,550
That's right, come!

10
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:41,010
I shall no longer be chained down by You!

11
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:46,730
I shall drag You down to earth and make You a part of me!

12
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:43,120
Is everyone okay?

13
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:44,040
What just happened?!

14
00:01:44,870 --> 00:01:47,620
A job well done, my dear sacrifices.

15
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:54,550
So you actually did it...!

16
00:01:55,090 --> 00:01:59,630
Yes, I've obtained God.

17
00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:01,260
'God', you say?!

18
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:02,640
Cut the bullshit-

19
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:04,680
It's possible.

20
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:07,350
If you're in possession of a tremendous amount of energy, that is.

21
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:08,520
Energy?

22
00:02:09,230 --> 00:02:10,230
A philosopher's stone!

23
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:12,150
You're joking!

24
00:02:12,150 --> 00:02:15,440
So you mean, everyone has already been turned into a philosopher's stone?!

25
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:18,240
Just how many lives were lost...?

26
00:02:19,450 --> 00:02:22,990
There are roughly 50 million people in this nation.

27
00:02:27,930 --> 00:02:30,930
He Who Would
 Swallow God

28
00:02:27,930 --> 00:02:30,930
He Who Would
 Swallow God

29
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,080
Son of a bitch!

30
00:02:35,210 --> 00:02:36,920
Shit!

31
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,840
I've sealed off alchemy.

32
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:40,930
Farewell, my friends.

33
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:44,470
That's...!

34
00:02:44,890 --> 00:02:47,520
Now that I've devoured God,

35
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:51,980
it's not impossible for me to create a sun in the palm of my hand.

36
00:02:57,940 --> 00:03:01,280
Should I let this loose right here and now?

37
00:03:05,370 --> 00:03:12,080
The turnabout had already begun from the moment you were in possession of Him.

38
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:22,590
For this day and for this day only,

39
00:03:22,590 --> 00:03:26,930
I had positioned my friends,
my philosopher's stones, all across the nation...

40
00:03:27,350 --> 00:03:30,390
...over a long period of time and with many calculations.

41
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:38,690
The time has come.

42
00:03:38,690 --> 00:03:42,450
He did something he shouldn't have done.

43
00:03:43,070 --> 00:03:46,450
We no longer have a body to return to.

44
00:03:46,450 --> 00:03:50,950
However, the people of Amestris do.

45
00:03:51,410 --> 00:03:56,710
Yes. Let us return their souls to their respective bodies.

46
00:03:57,170 --> 00:03:59,960
Hohenheim asked us to, after all.

47
00:04:01,880 --> 00:04:04,800
So all you did was to implant your philosopher's stones.

48
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,850
But those are just points.

49
00:04:06,850 --> 00:04:09,470
Without a circle, there is no alchemy.

50
00:04:09,470 --> 00:04:11,470
That's a basic principle of alchemy.

51
00:04:11,890 --> 00:04:13,560
But there IS a circle.

52
00:04:14,140 --> 00:04:21,990
A huge, powerful circle that'll activate by itself even if something were to happen to me!

53
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:28,120
The shadow of the moon that occurs from the solar eclipse!

54
00:04:29,660 --> 00:04:32,750
We'll be going on ahead, Hohenheim!

55
00:04:39,290 --> 00:04:43,760
You just continue to get in my way,
don't you, Hohenheim?!

56
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:46,430
That's precisely what I came here to do,

57
00:04:46,430 --> 00:04:49,760
Dwarf in the Flask, Homunculus!

58
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:19,350
Winry... are you okay?

59
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:21,810
What... just happened?

60
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:25,780
Did we lose consciousness?

61
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,030
It happened to you two as well?

62
00:06:28,030 --> 00:06:29,860
Looks like it.

63
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:32,030
But that was...

64
00:06:32,030 --> 00:06:34,450
How can I explain it... it was as if...

65
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:40,370
It felt like I was drowning in a whirlpool of suffering.

66
00:06:44,290 --> 00:06:45,380
Did it work?

67
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:50,590
The souls of the people of Amestris were returned to their respective bodies.

68
00:06:51,090 --> 00:06:58,310
He shouldn't be able to restrain this being he calls 'God' with only the souls of the people of Xerxes.

69
00:07:04,610 --> 00:07:07,110
I can just create another philosopher's stone.

70
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:10,070
A hundred million, or even a billion!

71
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:13,490
Humans, an energy form, are an unlimited source!{wow, disobeying the law of economics}{you are a dumb nigger}

72
00:07:30,090 --> 00:07:30,970
May!

73
00:07:31,970 --> 00:07:36,430
It's as easy as pie for an Eastern Alchemist to read and utilize the flow of the earth's energy!

74
00:07:36,430 --> 00:07:42,310
The more power he has, the more power we have that we can use as well!

75
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:44,900
Sir, look out!

76
00:07:52,450 --> 00:07:53,820
Dammit!

77
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:56,280
I don't have enough time to offset the energy!

78
00:07:58,870 --> 00:08:00,700
Please hold out!

79
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:02,370
The defense circle will be destroyed!

80
00:08:06,330 --> 00:08:07,460
It's impossible!

81
00:08:09,460 --> 00:08:11,420
Stand firm, Dad!

82
00:08:11,420 --> 00:08:14,800
You bastard, don't you dare give up!

83
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:19,260
Uh-oh.

84
00:08:19,260 --> 00:08:23,810
I'm a terrible father, but I want to make you two proud!

85
00:08:26,190 --> 00:08:29,730
If we don't hurry up, the philosopher's stone inside of Dad will run out!

86
00:08:31,070 --> 00:08:32,740
Hurry up, Scar!

87
00:08:34,610 --> 00:08:36,990
Ishbalan,

88
00:08:36,990 --> 00:08:39,870
I thought that alchemy, the reconstruction of matter,

89
00:08:39,870 --> 00:08:44,960
was a sin against Ishvala, the creator of all!

90
00:08:50,210 --> 00:08:52,340
Have you abandoned your god?!

91
00:08:56,720 --> 00:09:00,010
It seems as though...

92
00:09:02,810 --> 00:09:06,100
...'God' is hardly significant to you all!

93
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:07,230
Nay!

94
00:09:09,190 --> 00:09:11,690
After you learned the true meaning of despair...

95
00:09:15,610 --> 00:09:17,820
...during the Ishbalan War...!

96
00:09:22,790 --> 00:09:25,710
You must have realized somewhere inside of your heart!

97
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:29,710
God does not exist!

98
00:10:05,950 --> 00:10:09,210
I believed in neither destiny nor a god,

99
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:15,000
but one would probably look at this situation and say that the heavens are not on my side.

100
00:10:22,180 --> 00:10:25,470
The heavens brought forth a fitting visitor.

101
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:30,350
So you're here to avenge your grandfather...

102
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:32,980
That's fine as well.

103
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:34,650
Any last words?

104
00:10:35,110 --> 00:10:35,980
Nay.

105
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:38,780
A sad life you led.

106
00:10:39,530 --> 00:10:44,580
King Bradley, was there no one you loved?

107
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:46,540
Friends? Your wife?

108
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:49,460
Wife, eh...

109
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:52,960
You have no words to pass on to her?!

110
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,710
If she found out that you were a homunculus...!

111
00:10:55,130 --> 00:11:00,420
Brat, quit blabbering on about trifling topics such as love and sadness.

112
00:11:01,550 --> 00:11:03,550
Don't underestimate us.

113
00:11:03,550 --> 00:11:06,510
She's the woman I chose.

114
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:10,980
A will is unnecessary between us.

115
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:14,770
That's usually how it is between a King and his companion.

116
00:11:19,150 --> 00:11:25,740
Seems like you missed the chance to take revenge as you were caught up in foolish dialogue...

117
00:11:32,870 --> 00:11:37,170
Although my life was lived atop a rail which was already prepared for me...

118
00:11:37,590 --> 00:11:40,970
Thanks to you humans...

119
00:11:40,970 --> 00:11:49,020
...I feel like my life was somewhat worthwhile...

120
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:01,780
A sign of life?

121
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:05,070
It's a philosopher's stone.

122
00:12:06,240 --> 00:12:07,240
This?

123
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:11,080
Are you all right?!

124
00:12:13,830 --> 00:12:16,170
Please take me to that spot...

125
00:12:16,170 --> 00:12:17,960
The transmutation circle is broken!

126
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,260
It doesn't matter!

127
00:12:21,260 --> 00:12:23,930
That's the center of it all...!

128
00:12:23,930 --> 00:12:24,840
Got it.

129
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:38,110
Dear brother, to tell you the truth, I am not completely rid of hatred.

130
00:12:38,650 --> 00:12:43,740
Yet, I'm currently trying to help the ones
whom my hatred is directed at: the Amestrians.

131
00:12:45,110 --> 00:12:48,740
You once related it to the flow of positives and negatives,

132
00:12:49,490 --> 00:12:52,910
but where will I, who carry both of those conflicting elements,

133
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:58,670
be carried off to?!

134
00:13:14,060 --> 00:13:15,180
There it is!

135
00:13:29,530 --> 00:13:31,490
Serves you right.

136
00:13:31,490 --> 00:13:34,700
That chair you've been sitting high and mighty on is now in pieces.

137
00:13:36,250 --> 00:13:39,250
You've had your share of fun for your lifetime, bitch.

138
00:13:40,290 --> 00:13:44,010
I'll beat the shit out of both you and Truth!

139
00:13:52,050 --> 00:13:54,850
Was that... Eastern Alchemy?

140
00:13:54,850 --> 00:13:58,520
No, it's something my brother invented.

141
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:02,400
He used to research alchemy.

142
00:14:03,070 --> 00:14:07,530
And from there, he began to research Eastern Alchemy from Xing.

143
00:14:08,570 --> 00:14:12,530
Eastern Alchemy utilizes the flow of earth's energy.

144
00:14:13,780 --> 00:14:17,830
Alchemy from Amestris utilizes tectonic energy.

145
00:14:18,620 --> 00:14:21,540
But my brother realized...

146
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:25,880
...that alchemists are unable to use all of that power.

147
00:14:27,170 --> 00:14:31,930
There's something in the way between the alchemist and the tectonic energy.

148
00:14:32,930 --> 00:14:35,220
That feeling I got when I first came to this country...

149
00:14:35,770 --> 00:14:39,390
...it felt as though there were people crawling about underground.

150
00:14:39,980 --> 00:14:41,150
Right.

151
00:14:41,150 --> 00:14:46,860
It's probably the philosopher's stones that were stretched across underground.

152
00:14:56,120 --> 00:15:01,040
So Sir, the purpose of your transmutation circle was to return everyone's souls to their bodies?

153
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:03,880
Yeah, it worked out.

154
00:15:04,540 --> 00:15:10,380
And the purpose of the Turnabout Transmutation Circle Scar activated was to fix this nation's alchemy.

155
00:15:11,430 --> 00:15:17,180
After extensive research, Scar's brother began to doubt this nation's alchemy,

156
00:15:17,850 --> 00:15:21,690
and additionally, learned of the existence of the Nationwide Transmutation Circle.

157
00:15:22,810 --> 00:15:26,650
And with that at its base, and utilizing Eastern Alchemy for inscription,

158
00:15:26,650 --> 00:15:31,530
he created the Turnabout Transmutation Circle; one that would nullify the power of a philosopher's stone.

159
00:15:32,990 --> 00:15:37,280
And with this, alchemists are able to use all the tectonic energy to their liking,

160
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:38,950
something that used to be disrupted by philosopher's stones.

161
00:15:48,750 --> 00:15:50,800
Keep it up!

162
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:53,180
Make him use his philosopher's stone!

163
00:15:53,470 --> 00:15:55,390
He'll eventually run out of energy!

164
00:15:55,390 --> 00:15:57,470
And when'll that be?!

165
00:15:57,470 --> 00:15:58,470
I don't know!

166
00:15:58,470 --> 00:16:00,310
But all we can do is try!

167
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:01,770
Eat this!

168
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:15,110
This brings back memories.

169
00:16:15,110 --> 00:16:17,530
I remember bathing in that once.

170
00:16:17,530 --> 00:16:19,240
Why don't you take a soak too?

171
00:16:21,410 --> 00:16:22,790
Out of the way, Greed!

172
00:16:38,050 --> 00:16:38,850
Freeze!

173
00:16:39,350 --> 00:16:41,520
Now, slowly...

174
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:46,400
Lieutenant Hawkeye?

175
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:47,650
Major!

176
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:04,250
He must have gone up to create more philosopher's stones.

177
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:10,590
We're going after him.

178
00:17:10,590 --> 00:17:11,170
Right!

179
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,380
We'll get you somewhere safe too.

180
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:15,970
Sorry about this.

181
00:17:15,970 --> 00:17:18,300
Why am I so useless when people need me the most?

182
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:19,550
Brother!

183
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:22,220
You go on ahead, Al!

184
00:17:23,810 --> 00:17:26,520
Seems like he wants a piece of me.

185
00:17:30,730 --> 00:17:32,110
Let's go, Al.

186
00:17:32,650 --> 00:17:34,400
Don't die now, Ed!

187
00:17:34,610 --> 00:17:35,780
Yes'm!{lol}

188
00:17:41,030 --> 00:17:42,200
Dear!

189
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,620
Izumi!

190
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:47,830
We don't have time for this.

191
00:17:47,830 --> 00:17:48,870
Take care of the colonel.

192
00:17:49,080 --> 00:17:49,880
Right!

193
00:17:51,250 --> 00:17:52,130
Colonel!

194
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:57,130
There's someone that needs a real good spanking, so I'll be off!

195
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,300
Are you injured, Colonel?

196
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:02,010
They took my vision.

197
00:18:04,060 --> 00:18:07,230
What about your wounds, Lieutenant?

198
00:18:07,810 --> 00:18:09,600
Seriously...!

199
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:11,810
Please worry about yourself!

200
00:18:11,810 --> 00:18:12,270
Your eyes...!

201
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:15,030
Can you still fight?

202
00:18:19,150 --> 00:18:19,910
Yes!

203
00:18:28,290 --> 00:18:29,120
Young master!

204
00:18:29,120 --> 00:18:31,210
It's Greed.

205
00:18:31,210 --> 00:18:34,130
Geez, you followed us all the way down-

206
00:18:36,550 --> 00:18:37,590
Wrath!

207
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:42,600
So he bit the dust...

208
00:18:45,850 --> 00:18:48,230
You look so damn satisfied.

209
00:18:48,230 --> 00:18:49,440
Pisses me off.

210
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:52,020
Greed...!

211
00:18:52,020 --> 00:18:55,730
Throwing away his pride as a homunculus... how pathetic.

212
00:18:56,110 --> 00:19:00,320
Why are you guys so obedient towards a father like that?

213
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:03,320
What a stupid question.

214
00:19:03,820 --> 00:19:06,830
Isn't it obvious that we'd obey our own father?

215
00:19:07,910 --> 00:19:09,830
You're the stupid one here.

216
00:19:10,210 --> 00:19:12,040
"Obvious" you say?

217
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:15,590
You won't even try thinking with your own brain!

218
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:20,920
I don't get it...

219
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:24,090
Why do you continue to obey him?

220
00:19:25,050 --> 00:19:29,430
He doesn't give a damn even if you're badly hurt like that.

221
00:19:32,390 --> 00:19:34,900
So what?!

222
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:40,860
Don't apply this "common knowledge" of your human race to us homunculi!

223
00:19:48,620 --> 00:19:51,000
This container won't last for very much longer.

224
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:56,540
But since you, like our father,
have Hohenheim's blood in your veins,

225
00:19:56,540 --> 00:19:58,500
we're pretty much siblings.

226
00:19:59,050 --> 00:20:02,550
Edward Elric, give me your body...

227
00:20:02,550 --> 00:20:04,340
...a container!

228
00:20:06,510 --> 00:20:07,430
What?!

229
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:13,100
Unamused.

230
00:20:13,690 --> 00:20:17,980
I'm thoroughly unamused, homunculus Pride.

231
00:20:17,980 --> 00:20:20,610
Kimblee?! There's no way!

232
00:20:20,780 --> 00:20:25,240
How could you maintain your own self-awareness in this tempest of souls...?!

233
00:20:25,740 --> 00:20:27,450
Tempest?

234
00:20:27,450 --> 00:20:29,410
You make me giggle.

235
00:20:29,620 --> 00:20:33,870
Voices of resentment are like a lullaby to me.

236
00:20:35,670 --> 00:20:38,210
Why are you interfering with me, Kimblee?!

237
00:20:38,750 --> 00:20:46,340
Well, I wouldn't have done anything had you kept on fighting while conserving your pride as a homunculus.

238
00:20:46,510 --> 00:20:50,850
However, first, you blab on about your pride as a homunculus,

239
00:20:50,850 --> 00:20:53,980
then just as your life is in danger,

240
00:20:53,980 --> 00:20:59,310
you proceed to escape into the container of a human, a being you looked down on as inferior.

241
00:20:59,310 --> 00:21:00,230
You...

242
00:21:01,070 --> 00:21:02,480
...lack elegance.

243
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:12,540
I'm going to be killed!

244
00:21:13,830 --> 00:21:17,670
You don't understand Edward Elric!

245
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:27,300
Selim!!

246
00:21:27,590 --> 00:21:28,550
Impossible...!

247
00:21:28,550 --> 00:21:32,640
He turned himself into a philosopher's stone to infiltrate me?!

248
00:21:35,310 --> 00:21:37,640
I've got you now, Selim!

249
00:21:38,190 --> 00:21:39,270
Stop...

250
00:21:41,270 --> 00:21:42,110
Stop...!

251
00:21:43,980 --> 00:21:48,610
Please, stop!!

252
00:22:06,340 --> 00:22:08,130
So this is your true self.

253
00:22:10,470 --> 00:22:15,310
I'd better go and apologize to Madam Bradley after all this is over.

254
00:22:16,890 --> 00:22:19,770
Just wait there, stupid brat.

255
00:22:24,530 --> 00:22:28,360
Mommy... Mommy...

256
00:22:41,630 --> 00:22:45,180
Ever since that day passed,

257
00:22:41,630 --> 00:22:45,180
Ano hi kara zutto

258
00:22:45,180 --> 00:22:49,430
I promised myself that I'd never cry.

259
00:22:45,180 --> 00:22:49,430
Nakanaito kimetekitakedo

260
00:22:49,970 --> 00:22:54,980
But even while I hoarded up the pain,

261
00:22:49,970 --> 00:22:54,980
Itami wo kasanetemo

262
00:22:54,980 --> 00:23:00,090
there was something I couldn't forgive myself for.

263
00:22:54,980 --> 00:23:00,090
Nanika wo yurusezu ni ita

264
00:23:01,570 --> 00:23:03,530
I'll never be able

265
00:23:01,570 --> 00:23:03,530
Mou modorenai

266
00:23:03,530 --> 00:23:06,030
to return to those days.

267
00:23:03,530 --> 00:23:06,030
Ikutsumo no hibi

268
00:23:06,030 --> 00:23:11,120
I'm still powerless.

269
00:23:06,030 --> 00:23:11,120
Boku wa mada nanimo dekizuni

270
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:16,370
I watch as the shards of memories disappear, one by one;

271
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:16,370
Kimi no ita kioku no kakera

272
00:23:16,370 --> 00:23:22,240
memories of when you were still with me.

273
00:23:16,370 --> 00:23:22,240
Mata hitotsu kieteyuku

274
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:25,260
I long to become

275
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:25,260
Kyou yori motto

276
00:23:25,260 --> 00:23:28,010
stronger than I am now,

277
00:23:25,260 --> 00:23:28,010
Tsuyoku naritai

278
00:23:28,010 --> 00:23:33,150
so that my voice will eventually reach you.

279
00:23:28,010 --> 00:23:33,150
Kono koe ga itsuka todokuyouni

280
00:23:33,150 --> 00:23:35,520
If the wind happens to stop

281
00:23:33,150 --> 00:23:35,520
Arukitsuzukete

282
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:38,230
in the midst of my long journey,

283
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:38,230
Kaze ga yandara

284
00:23:38,230 --> 00:23:42,940
I'll look up at the sky in search of you.

285
00:23:38,230 --> 00:23:42,940
Kimi wo sagashite sora miageruyo

286
00:23:43,690 --> 00:23:50,280
Beyond the daybreak, a ray of light breaks free.

287
00:23:43,690 --> 00:23:50,280
Yoake no saki ni hikari ga sasuyo

288
00:23:51,450 --> 00:23:55,830
A rainbow spans across the sky.

289
00:23:51,450 --> 00:23:55,830
Niji ga kakaruyo

290
00:23:59,290 --> 00:24:02,540
The strong arms roars; the flame thunders forth.

291
00:24:02,960 --> 00:24:07,540
Staking their existence, the people give their full measure!

292
00:24:07,540 --> 00:24:11,800
Yes! The final battle is now here!

293
00:24:12,510 --> 00:24:16,510
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

294
00:24:16,510 --> 00:24:21,020
Episode 62, A Fierce Counterattack.

295
00:24:16,530 --> 00:24:21,030
A Fierce Counterattack

296
00:24:21,020 --> 00:24:25,740
If one wishes to gain something,
one must present something of equal value.
